      "writtenOn": "2024-05-14T10:44:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As suggested by the assert message, the check should run in the policy level (if this evaluates to `false` it crashes anyway). In this patch series, the policy disables LE (i.e., does not initialize `LeAudioClient`) unless the chrome flag `CrOSLateBootBluetoothAudioLEAudioOnly` is enabled.\n\nNote that it is `enable_profile -\u003e enable -\u003e self.internal.pin_mut().init()` that initializes `LeAudioClient`, where `self.le_audio.as_mut().unwrap().initialize(le_audio_dispatcher);` doesn\u0027t do much (see https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/3081368/1/system/gd/rust/topshim/src/profiles/le_audio.rs#555).\n\nTo be extra sure, I\u0027ve also verified on a Cherry that with this patch series and leaving the LeAudio flag as default, classic audio functions are working. Thanks for the heads up!",
      "parentUuid": "db2d2b86_918446a1",
